# Fake News Detection System

An end-to-end **Fake News Detection web application** that uses Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Machine Learning to classify news headlines as **Fake** or **Real**. The application is built with Flask and also retrieves related articles from **NewsAPI** and **GDELT** to provide additional context for users.

---

## Overview

The system combines:

* NLP-based text preprocessing
* TF-IDF feature extraction
* Logistic Regression classification
* GridSearchCV-based hyperparameter tuning
* Flask web application
* NewsAPI integration
* GDELT API integration

A user can enter a news headline through the web interface. The application processes the headline using the trained ML pipeline, predicts whether it is fake or real, and then fetches related articles from external news sources.

> **Important:** The model predicts based on patterns learned from its training data. It does not independently verify the factual truth of a news claim.

---

## Key Features

* **Fake News Classification** using Logistic Regression
* **Natural Language Processing** for text preprocessing
* Removal of non-alphabetic characters
* Lowercasing and tokenization
* English stopword removal
* Porter stemming
* **TF-IDF Vectorization**
* **GridSearchCV** for hyperparameter optimization
* Stratified train-test split
* Persistent model and vectorizer using Joblib
* Flask-based web interface
* Real-time headline prediction
* Related article retrieval using NewsAPI
* Additional article retrieval using GDELT
* Article deduplication
* Input validation and API error handling

---

